    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "blev sendt or var sendt",
     "texto": [
      "Both mean «was sent», but:\n\n- **blev** + participle = the **action**: Hvornår **blev** pakken sendt? (When was the parcel sent?)\n- **var** + participle = the **state**: Pakken **var** sendt. (It had already been sent.)\n\nLike «the door was opened» (action) versus «the door was open» (state)."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "🗣 Your turn to speak (A2)",
     "texto": [
      "These blocks are **oral tasks at A2 level**: things you may be asked to tell, ask or give opinions about.\n\n- Read the task.\n- Press «🙈 Just listen» and listen to the sentences.\n- Say **your** sentences out loud and compare.\n\nYou'll also find them in the **Phrases** section."
     ],
     "tutora": "contenta"
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Swearing: handle with care",
     "texto": [
      "Danish swear words are mostly about religion rather than sex. A few more:\n\n- **Av for katten / Søren / Pokker!** = Oh dear! (mild)\n- *Av for Fanden / Satan / Helvede!* = stronger now.\n- **skidt** is only mild (Skidt med det!), but *skidedum* (very stupid) or *skidetosset* (furious) sound vulgar.\n\nTip from the book: swearing in another language is difficult; if you get it wrong, you'll just sound odd."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
